 "beats": [
  {
   "type": "title",
   "speaker": "q",
   "scene": "globe",
   "text": "Which English word comes from Spain's war against Napoleon?"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Guerrilla. It means little war, and Spain fought one against the greatest army in Europe."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "Where did it start?",
   "scene": "start",
   "date": "1808",
   "place": "Spain"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "In July 1808, at Bailén, a Spanish army forced a whole French corps to surrender. A Napoleonic army had never lost an open battle like this.",
   "scene": "bailen",
   "date": "19 July 1808",
   "place": "Bailén",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.4,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.55,
     0.5,
     1.25
    ]
   },
   "say": "In July 1808, at Bylen, a Spanish army forced a whole French corps to surrender. A Napoleonic army had never lost an open battle like this."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "What did Napoleon do?"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Joseph fled Madrid. Napoleon came himself, with a huge army."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Zaragoza held out through two sieges, street by street. When the gunners fell, a young woman, Agustina, fired the cannon herself.",
   "scene": "agustina",
   "date": "1808 – 1809",
   "place": "Zaragoza",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.5,
     0.45,
     1.3
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "So where does guerrilla come from?",
   "scene": "guerrilla",
   "date": ""
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "All over Spain, small bands ambushed the French and vanished. Spaniards called it guerrilla: the little war."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Both sides were brutal. Goya etched it all. The prints were so dark, they came out only after his death.",
   "scene": "disaster",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.5,
     0.45,
     1.3
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "How did the French finally lose?",
   "scene": "wellington",
   "date": "21 June 1813",
   "place": "Vitoria",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.4,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.5,
     0.33,
     1.3
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "With the British under Wellington, they were crushed at Vitoria in 1813. King Joseph ran for France."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "So Spain was free again?",
   "scene": "end",
   "date": "1814",
   "place": "Spain"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Yes. Then Ferdinand came home. Spaniards had died in his name. He thanked them by tearing up their new constitution.",
   "scene": "ferdinand",
   "date": "4 May 1814",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.4,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.5,
     0.33,
     1.25
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "They had fought for their king. Their king did not fight for them.",
   "scene": "tresmayo",
   "date": "",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.55,
     0.5,
     1.2
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Next time: the constitution written under siege. Like the video and follow History Sketches."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "And tell us in the comments what you think!"
  },
  {
   "type": "end",
   "text": "Next: the constitution written under siege",
   "sub": "Follow History Sketches"
  }
 ],
